[07:59:19] [INFO] THE PHYSICS:
[07:59:19] [INFO] ============
[07:59:19] [INFO] From manuscript 12 (TEP-H0), the TEP effect operates on CLOCK RATES via
[07:59:19] [INFO] the conformal factor A(Φ) ≈ 1 - ηΦ/c², where Φ is the gravitational potential.
[07:59:19] [INFO] 
[07:59:19] [INFO] For pulsar period: P_obs = P_true × A(Φ) (period contraction in deep potentials)
[07:59:19] [INFO] 
[07:59:19] [INFO] This is fundamentally different from Newtonian gravity, where the
[07:59:19] [INFO] observable Ṗ excess comes from cluster acceleration a = GM/r².
[07:59:19] [INFO] 
[07:59:19] [INFO] SCALING ANALYSIS:
[07:59:19] [INFO] ================
[07:59:19] [INFO] For self-gravitating clusters:
[07:59:19] [INFO] - Central density: ρ_c ∝ M/R_c³
[07:59:19] [INFO] - Acceleration (Newtonian): a ∝ GM/R_c² ∝ ρ_c × R_c
[07:59:19] [INFO] - Potential (TEP): |Φ| ∝ GM/R_c ∝ ρ_c × R_c²
[07:59:19] [INFO] 
[07:59:19] [INFO] Across the cluster sample, let the effective scaling relationship between
[07:59:19] [INFO] core radius and density be characterized by the OLS regression slope:
[07:59:19] [INFO] α_eff = Cov(log R_c, log ρ_c) / Var(log ρ_c)
[07:59:19] [INFO] 
[07:59:19] [INFO] By the exact linearity of covariance:
[07:59:19] [INFO]   Γ_N = Cov(log a, log ρ) / Var(log ρ) = 1 + α_eff
[07:59:19] [INFO]   Γ_TEP = Cov(log |Φ|, log ρ) / Var(log ρ) = 1 + 2α_eff
[07:59:19] [INFO] 
[07:59:19] [INFO] ELIMINATING α_eff:
[07:59:19] [INFO] ==============
[07:59:19] [INFO] From Γ_N = 1 + α_eff, we get α_eff = Γ_N - 1
[07:59:19] [INFO] Substituting: Γ_TEP = 1 + 2(Γ_N - 1) = 2Γ_N - 1
[07:59:19] [INFO] 
[07:59:19] [INFO] This is an EXACT mathematical identity for regression slopes!
[07:59:19] [INFO] 
